/// The rig's protocol bot (P4.8, CAL-42): one player who runs a scenario against a running
/// server, as a vanilla 26.3 client would, and writes down every packet the server sends, so
/// `rig/runner/sessions.py` can compare what vanilla and Calcite each sent. It's made from
/// Calcite's protocol code, as the bot benchmark's players are, but what it's sent is read with
/// vanilla's own codecs (D145), so it agrees with neither server on a mistake.
///
///     calx run --release src/rig/session.calx -- PORT VIEW SCENARIO OUT
///
/// The scenarios:
///
/// - `status`: the server list's query, then a ping.
/// - `outdated`: a login from a client one protocol version behind.
/// - `bad-name`: a login with a name no vanilla client sends.
/// - `stranger`: a login from a player who isn't on the whitelist.
/// - `join`: an offline login, configuration knowing vanilla's core pack, then play: the bot
///   loads its view, `VIEW` chunks from the center, walks into the next chunk a block a tick,
///   says something, types a command no server has, and leaves.
/// - `watch`: as `join`, but then the bot stays where it is, in a step of its own from play's
///   start, and leaves once the server's time is `WATCH` ticks past what it was at the join, as
///   the first `set_time` after that says, which is the last packet it records. A world whose
///   blocks keep changing, redstone running, never goes quiet for a step to end (CAL-116).
/// - `creative`: as `join`, but once its view's loaded, in a step of its own, the bot, in creative
///   mode, sets slots of its inventory menu as the creative menu does: stacks put in, armor put
///   on, slots emptied, a stack with a component set and one with a component taken away, a slot
///   that isn't one and a stack too big, which a server lets be; then it leaves (CAL-135).
/// - `clicks`: as `join`, but once its view's loaded, the bot, in survival mode, clicks in its
///   inventory menu, each click in a step of its own named for it, with the menu's state as the
///   server last sent it and the slots a client would say the click changed, by their stacks'
///   hashes: stacks picked up, put down, halved, merged, shift-clicked, swapped with a hotbar key,
///   put in the crafting grid and on and off the head, a click whose cursor it gets wrong, one
///   from a state that's gone, and a drag; then it closes the menu and leaves (CAL-136).
/// - `dig`: as `join`, but once its view's loaded, the bot, in survival mode, digs the dig
///   fixture's blocks, each in a step of its own named for it, as a client's player actions say,
///   each with the next sequence number: the ground under spawn protection; the ground started and
///   stopped at once, so the server digs it the rest of the way; started and aborted, started then
///   another started, aborted elsewhere, stopped elsewhere, and out of reach; a tripwire cut with
///   shears; the dirt under the first with a pickaxe that breaks as it does; and its hands
///   swapped; then it leaves (D376).
/// - `dig-creative`: as `dig`, in creative mode: the ground, a bed's foot, a door's top, tall
///   grass's top and a command block broken, then the ground with a sword, which doesn't (D376).
/// - `place`: as `dig`, but the bot places blocks by the place fixture's, each use of an item on a
///   block in a step of its own named for it, with the next sequence number: stone on the ground,
///   where it stands, in short grass, from the offhand, on a lectern, which takes the use, and on
///   stone; stairs, and stairs on their side's top half; a slab, then another into it, and one in
///   water; a log on its side; a door, a bed, a torch on a wall and on the floor; a fence, then
///   another beside it; a furnace turned west; then a use out of reach and one hitting far from
///   its block (D378); then it crouches, places stone on the lectern, which crouching doesn't
///   use, and stands (CAL-141).
/// - `place-creative`: as `place`, in creative mode, with each block's item given it as the
///   creative menu does: blocks turned as the player looks, joined to the blocks beside them,
///   attached to a side or falling back to the floor (D378).
/// - `use`: as `place`, with nothing in its hands, using the use fixture's blocks, each use in a
///   step of its own: a door opened, shut and opened from its top, an iron door that won't, a
///   trapdoor, a fence gate opened away and shut, a lever pulled on and off and a button pressed,
///   each lighting a lamp, a button pressed again while it's down, a repeater's delay and a
///   comparator's mode turned, a note block tuned, a bell rung from its side and not from its top,
///   a daylight detector inverted, and redstone dust turned to a cross and back (D379).
/// - `use-items`: as `use`, using items on the use_items fixture's blocks, each use in a step of
///   its own: seeds and a cake composted, a sapling potted, its full pot, and the sapling taken
///   back, a candle put out, a candle on a cake, the candle cake and the cake eaten, a cauldron
///   filled by a water bucket, a water bottle taken and poured back, a helmet's dye and a banner's
///   last pattern washed off, a bucket a low cauldron won't fill, and a bucket of lava (CAL-142).
/// - `use-books`: as `use-items`, on the same fixture's lectern, chiseled bookshelf and decorated
///   pot: a book and quill on the lectern, a book and an enchanted book in the bookshelf's slots,
///   the book taken back, an empty slot and the top used, and stone put in the pot twice, dirt that
///   won't go in, and the pot used by hand (CAL-142); then a record put in the fixture's jukebox,
///   which plays it, stone put on its shelf, swapped for dirt, the dirt taken back, an empty slot
///   used by hand, the hotbar swapped with the powered shelves', and the record taken out
///   (CAL-143).
/// - `use-containers`: as `use`, opening the containers fixture's containers, each opened, clicked
///   in and closed in a step of its own, the clicks with the menu's state as the server sends it
///   first, so all of a step's packets come in one tick, before its lid's recheck: a chest's
///   diamonds taken, put in the inventory and stone shift-clicked in; iron shift-clicked out of a
///   large chest's left half; a trapped chest by a lamp opened and closed; half a barrel's
///   cobblestone taken and the menu closed with it carried; dirt shift-clicked into the ender
///   chest; cobblestone into a shulker box; a dispenser's arrows shift-clicked out; a hopper
///   opened, then a chest while it's open; and a chest under stone, which won't open (CAL-144).
/// - `items`: as `use`, dropping and throwing items, each in a step of its own: one of the held
///   stack dropped, the next slot's dropped whole, logs picked up and thrown out of the inventory
///   menu, one then the rest, which merge, stone thrown east from its slot with the throw key, one
///   then all, which merge, and a sword dropped looking west and down; then two steps that wait,
///   each typing a command no server has, for the items' pickup delay, a walk south over the
///   items, which picks them up, and a last wait. Stacks that merge are thrown in the same step,
///   so they come in the same tick on both servers, and are of different sizes, so which goes
///   into which doesn't turn on which of them looks first (CAL-148).
/// - `items-saved`: as `use`, on a world with items saved in it: two steps that wait, a walk
///   south over them, which picks up those it may, and a last wait (CAL-148).
/// - `orbs`: as `use`, with a diamond hoe with mending: three sculk broken at once, each worth an
///   orb of 1, then a sculk catalyst dug through, worth 5, with steps that wait between, for the
///   orbs to follow it and be picked up (CAL-154).
/// - `feed`: as `use`, holding wheat, feeding the feed fixture's animals by the order the server
///   sent them, each use of an entity in a step of its own, timed by the server's clock, as the
///   animals never settle: sent on the first `set_time` at or past its game time, which marks the
///   step's start, so each comes between the same two ticks on both servers. The first cow, the
///   second and the third, a calf and two grown, so the grown pair falls in love; both sheep; the
///   first cow again; then a step, `breed`, from a game time too, while they breed, their orbs
///   come to the bot and their babies grow, and it leaves at a game time (CAL-158, D415).
/// - `attack`: as `feed`, with its hand empty and a stone axe in its hotbar's second slot, hitting
///   the attack fixture's animals by the server's clock, a hit sent with another in the same
///   batch landing in the same tick, so its cooldown shrugs that off: the first cow punched twice,
///   the axe taken, the sheep chopped twice, the cow killed, the sheep killed, the second cow
///   chopped and killed; then a step as their loot lies and their orbs come to it, and a hit on
///   the first item the server sent, which has it disconnected (CAL-162, D416).
/// - `sweep`: as `attack`, with an iron sword, at the sweep fixture's animals side by side: the
///   sheep swept, and hit again in the same tick, too weak to; sprinting started, then the first
///   cow hit as it sprints, a knockback attack, which stops it; then each swept till they're dead,
///   and a step as their loot lies and their orbs come, till it leaves (D417).
/// - `fall`: in survival with an iron sword, falls onto honey, into water and onto stone, hitting a
///   cow as it falls, a critical hit (D418).
/// - `checks`: in survival by a stone wall, a move too quick, which the server sends it back
///   from; one through the wall, wrong; one into it, which meets it anew; up by a ladder and
///   down past it fast, which resets its fall (D422); then up into the air, where it floats till
///   the server kicks it (D420).
///
/// OUT gets each packet in the order it came: its state's number, as vanilla's
/// `ConnectionProtocol` orders them from handshake at 0, its length as 4 bytes, big-endian, then
/// its ID and fields, as `src/test/play.calx` writes them for `PacketCheck`. A record whose
/// state is 255 is a mark instead, whose bytes are text: `step NAME` as the bot starts each step,
/// `closed` when the server closes the connection, and `timeout` if a step waited too long.
/// The bot ends a step once the server has sent nothing for a second but the time and
/// keep-alives, which vanilla sends on a clock, and entities' moves, which vanilla's mobs never
/// stop sending where Calcite has none (D377), so both servers' steps hold the same packets.
module rig.session

import hash.ops.{hash_map, hash_string}
import java.uuid.{Uuid}
import pack.resources.{KnownPack}
import protocol.chat.{LastSeenUpdate, ServerboundChat, ServerboundChatCommand}
import protocol.codec.{Codec}
import protocol.common.{ChatVisibility, ClientInformation, HumanoidArm, ParticleStatus, ServerboundClientInformation, ServerboundCustomPayload, ServerboundKeepAlive, ServerboundPong}
import protocol.configuration.{ServerboundFinishConfiguration, ServerboundSelectKnownPacks}
import protocol.handshake.{ClientIntent, ClientIntention}
import protocol.ids.{PROTOCOL_VERSION, packet_names}
import protocol.login.{ServerboundHello, ServerboundLoginAcknowledged}
import protocol.play.{PERFORM_RESPAWN, ServerboundAcceptTeleportation, ServerboundAttack, ServerboundChunkBatchReceived, ServerboundClientCommand, ServerboundClientTickEnd, ServerboundContainerClick, ServerboundContainerClose, ServerboundInteract, ServerboundMovePlayerPos, ServerboundMovePlayerPosRot, ServerboundMovePlayerRot, ServerboundPlayerAction, ServerboundPlayerCommand, ServerboundPlayerInput, ServerboundPlayerLoaded, ServerboundSetCarriedItem, ServerboundSetCreativeModeSlot, ServerboundUseItemOn, ON_GROUND}
import protocol.state.{State, Bound}
import protocol.status.{ServerboundPingRequest, ServerboundStatusRequest}
import protocol.wire.{Reader, Writer, Wire, Packet, write_packet}
import registry.builtin.{builtin_entries, builtin_names}
import resources.identifier.{Identifier}
import server.chunks.{in_view_count}
import std.env.{args}
import std.fs.{write}
import std.net.{Net, Conn, Event}
import std.time.{Instant}
import world.pos.{BlockPos}

const TICK_NS: u64 = 50000000
const MS: u64 = 1000000
// How long the server must send nothing but its clock's packets for a step to end.
const SETTLE: u64 = 1000000000
// How long a step may take before the bot gives up on it.
const STEP_LIMIT: u64 = 20000000000
// The chunks a tick the bot asks for, as the bot benchmark's players do.
const DESIRED: f32 = 25.0
// The blocks the bot walks, a block a tick, which takes it into the next chunk.
const WALK: i32 = 16
// The game ticks `watch` watches the world for, from the time at the join.
const WATCH: i64 = 400
// When the bot says it sent its chat message, in milliseconds since 1970: a fixed time, so both
// servers are sent the same message.
const CHAT_TIME: i64 = 1800000000000

fn number(s: String) -> u64 {
    var n: u64 = 0
    for i in 0..s.len() {
        let b = s.byte_at(i)
        if b < 48 or b > 57 {
            panic("{s} isn't a number")
        }
        n = n * 10 + u64(b - 48)
    }
    return n
}

fn packet<T: Wire + Packet>(p: T, state: State) -> List<u8> {
    var w = Writer.new()
    write_packet(p, state, mut w)
    return w.into_bytes()
}

fn state_number(state: State) -> u8 {
    return match state {
        State.Handshake => 0,
        State.Status => 1,
        State.Login => 2,
        State.Configuration => 3,
        State.Play => 4,
    }
}

// What the bot is doing in play.
enum Phase {
    // Not in play yet, or not in a scenario that plays.
    Before
    // Loading its view after joining.
    Join
    // Walking, with how many blocks are left.
    Walk
    Chat
    Command
    // Setting creative slots, in `creative`.
    Creative
    // Clicking in the inventory menu, in `clicks`.
    Clicks
    // Digging blocks, in `dig` and `dig-creative`, or placing them, in `place` and `place-creative`.
    Dig
    // It has closed the connection.
    Leave
}

struct Bot {
    scenario: String
    conn: Conn
    codec: Codec
    state: State
    closed: bool = false
    // Every record, as the file gets them.
    out: Writer
    phase: Phase = Phase.Before
    // When the current step began, and when the server last sent something off its clock.
    step_at: u64 = 0
    heard_at: u64 = 0
    placed: bool = false
    loaded: bool = false
    x: f64 = 0.0
    y: f64 = 0.0
    z: f64 = 0.0
    chunks: u64 = 0
    // The bot's entity, once its death's told, which it respawns from once it's out of its level,
    // as a player clicks the death screen's button once it's there (D428).
    dead: i32 = -1
    walked: i32 = 0
    done: bool = false
    // In `watch`, the game time at the join, from the first `set_time`, or -1 before it.
    joined_at: i64 = -1
    // The inventory menu's state, as the server last sent it, and in `clicks`, the click it's at;
    // and the state of the container's menu last sent (CAL-144).
    menu_state: i32 = 0
    box_state: i32 = 0
    click_at: usize = 0
    // In `dig`, `dig-creative`, `place` and `place-creative`, the step it's at.
    dig_at: usize = 0
    // The moves a step is still to make, one a tick, as a client sends at most one position a
    // tick (CAL-148).
    moves: List<(f64, f64, f64)> = List<(f64, f64, f64)>()
    // The cows, sheep and items the server sent, by their entity IDs, in the order it sent them,
    // and the types they're sent as (CAL-158, D416); the steps the server's clock times still to
    // come, each its game time, its name, empty for one that goes on with the last, and what it
    // sends, in the order they come; and the game time the bot leaves at, -1 for none (D415).
    cows: List<i32> = List<i32>()
    sheep: List<i32> = List<i32>()
    items: List<i32> = List<i32>()
    cow_type: i32 = -1
    sheep_type: i32 = -1
    item_type: i32 = -1
    timed: List<(i64, String, Timed)> = List<(i64, String, Timed)>()
    leave_at: i64 = -1
}

impl Bot {
    fn send(mut self, net: Net, p: own List<u8>) {
        if not self.closed {
            net.write(self.conn, self.codec.encode(p)!)
        }
    }

    fn record(mut self, state: u8, bytes: List<u8>) {
        self.out.u8(state)
        self.out.i32(i32.wrap(bytes.len()))
        self.out.raw(bytes)
    }

    fn mark(mut self, text: String) {
        self.record(255, text.to_bytes())
    }

    fn step(mut self, name: String, now: u64) {
        self.mark("step {name}")
        self.step_at = now
        self.heard_at = now
    }

    // Opens the connection the way the scenario starts.
    fn start(mut self, net: Net, port: u16) {
        if self.scenario == "status" {
            self.step(String("status"), 0)
            self.send(net, packet(ClientIntention { protocol_version: PROTOCOL_VERSION, host_name: "localhost", port: port, intention: ClientIntent.Status }, State.Handshake))
            self.state = State.Status
            self.send(net, packet(ServerboundStatusRequest {}, State.Status))
            return
        }
        let version = if self.scenario == "outdated" { PROTOCOL_VERSION - 1 } else { PROTOCOL_VERSION }
        let name = if self.scenario == "bad-name" { String("bad name!") } else if self.scenario == "stranger" { String("Stranger") } else { String("Bot") }
        self.step(String("login"), 0)
        self.send(net, packet(ClientIntention { protocol_version: version, host_name: "localhost", port: port, intention: ClientIntent.Login }, State.Handshake))
        self.state = State.Login
        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundHello { name: name, profile_id: Uuid.new(0, 0) }, State.Login))
    }

    // Records and answers what came, at `now`.
    fn handle(mut self, net: Net, now: u64) {
        loop {
            let body = match self.codec.next() {
                ok(some(b)) => b,
                ok(none) => return,
                err(_) => {
                    self.mark(String("undecodable"))
                    self.closed = true
                    self.done = true
                    return
                },
            }
            let at = state_number(self.state)
            self.record(at, body)
            var r = Reader.new(body)
            let id = usize.wrap(r.varint()!)
            let names = packet_names(self.state, Bound.Clientbound)
            let name = if id < names.len() { names[id].copy() } else { String("?") }
            if not quiet(name) {
                self.heard_at = now
            }
            match self.state {
                State.Status => {
                    if name == "status_response" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPingRequest { time: 1234 }, State.Status))
                    } else if name == "pong_response" {
                        net.close(self.conn)
                        self.closed = true
                    }
                },
                State.Login => {
                    if name == "login_compression" {
                        self.codec.start_compression(r.varint()!)
                    } else if name == "login_finished" {
                        // A vanilla client acknowledges, then sends its brand and settings.
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundLoginAcknowledged {}, State.Login))
                        self.state = State.Configuration
                        self.step(String("configuration"), now)
                        var brand = Writer.new()
                        brand.string("vanilla", 32767)
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundCustomPayload { channel: Identifier { namespace: "minecraft", path: "brand" }, payload: brand.into_bytes() }, State.Configuration))
                        let info = ClientInformation { language: "en_us", view_distance: 12, chat_visibility: ChatVisibility.Full, chat_colors: true, model_customisation: 127, main_hand: HumanoidArm.Right, text_filtering_enabled: false, allows_listing: true, particle_status: ParticleStatus.All }
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundClientInformation { information: info }, State.Configuration))
                    }
                },
                State.Configuration => {
                    if name == "select_known_packs" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundSelectKnownPacks { packs: [KnownPack { namespace: "minecraft", id: "core", version: "26.3" }] }, State.Configuration))
                    } else if name == "keep_alive" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundKeepAlive { challenge: r.i64()! }, State.Configuration))
                    } else if name == "ping" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPong { token: r.i32()! }, State.Configuration))
                    } else if name == "finish_configuration" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundFinishConfiguration {}, State.Configuration))
                        self.state = State.Play
                        self.phase = Phase.Join
                        let first = String(if self.watching() { "watch" } else { "join" })
                        self.step(first, now)
                    }
                },
                State.Play => {
                    if name == "keep_alive" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundKeepAlive { challenge: r.i64()! }, State.Play))
                    } else if name == "ping" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPong { token: r.i32()! }, State.Play))
                    } else if name == "player_position" {
                        // A vanilla client accepts the teleport, then says where it is.
                        let teleport = r.varint()!
                        self.x = r.f64()!
                        self.y = r.f64()!
                        self.z = r.f64()!
                        let accept = packet(ServerboundAcceptTeleportation { teleport_id: teleport, x: self.x, y: self.y, z: self.z, y_rot: 0.0, x_rot: 0.0 }, State.Play)
                        self.send(net, accept)
                        let moved = packet(ServerboundMovePlayerPosRot { x: self.x, y: self.y, z: self.z, y_rot: 0.0, x_rot: 0.0, flags: ON_GROUND }, State.Play)
                        self.send(net, moved)
                        self.placed = true
                    } else if name == "container_set_content" or name == "container_set_slot" {
                        // A client's menu takes the state the server sends with its slots.
                        let window = r.varint()!
                        let state = r.varint()!
                        if window == 0 {
                            self.menu_state = state
                        } else {
                            self.box_state = state
                        }
                    } else if name == "player_combat_kill" {
                        self.dead = r.varint()!
                    } else if name == "entity_event" and self.dead >= 0 {
                        // Its entity event 60, as it's taken out of its level: it asks to respawn
                        // (D428).
                        let entity = r.i32()!
                        let event = r.i8()!
                        if entity == self.dead and event == 60i8 {
                            self.dead = -1
                            self.send(net, packet(ServerboundClientCommand { action: PERFORM_RESPAWN }, State.Play))
                        }
                    } else if name == "respawn" {
                        // A client that respawns loads the chunks around it again before it says
                        // it's loaded (D428).
                        self.chunks = 0
                        self.loaded = false
                    } else if name == "level_chunk_with_light" {
                        self.chunks += 1
                    } else if name == "chunk_batch_finished" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundChunkBatchReceived { desired_chunks_per_tick: DESIRED }, State.Play))
                    } else if name == "add_entity" {
                        // `ClientboundAddEntityPacket`: its ID, its UUID, then its type.
                        let entity = r.varint()!
                        _ = r.i64()!
                        _ = r.i64()!
                        let kind = r.varint()!
                        if kind == self.cow_type {
                            self.cows.push(entity)
                        } else if kind == self.sheep_type {
                            self.sheep.push(entity)
                        } else if kind == self.item_type {
                            self.items.push(entity)
                        }
                    } else if name == "set_time" and (not self.timed.is_empty() or self.leave_at >= 0) {
                        // The steps due by the server's clock, each with what it sends, then the
                        // leave once they've come and it's due (D415).
                        let time = r.i64()!
                        while not self.timed.is_empty() and self.timed[0].0 <= time {
                            let (_, step, act) = self.timed.remove(0)
                            if not step.is_empty() {
                                self.step(step, now)
                            }
                            self.act(net, act)
                        }
                        if self.timed.is_empty() and self.leave_at >= 0 and time >= self.leave_at {
                            self.step(String("leave"), now)
                            net.close(self.conn)
                            self.closed = true
                            self.done = true
                            return
                        }
                    } else if name == "set_time" and self.watching() {
                        let time = r.i64()!
                        if self.joined_at < 0 {
                            self.joined_at = time
                        } else if time >= self.joined_at + WATCH {
                            self.step(String("leave"), now)
                            net.close(self.conn)
                            self.closed = true
                            self.done = true
                            return
                        }
                    }
                },
                _ => {},
            }
        }
    }

    // The click `click_at` of `clicks`, in a step of its own: each of its packets, a click from the
    // menu's state, or from 0 where it's stale, or a close.
    fn click(mut self, net: Net, now: u64) {
        let c = clicks()[self.click_at].copy()
        self.step(c.name.copy(), now)
        for p in c.packets {
            if p.close {
                self.send(net, packet(ServerboundContainerClose { container_id: 0 }, State.Play))
                continue
            }
            var rest = Writer.new()
            rest.varint(i32.wrap(p.changed.len()))
            for (slot, stack) in p.changed {
                rest.i16(slot)
                rest.raw(stack)
            }
            rest.raw(p.carried)
            let state = if p.stale { 0 } else { self.menu_state }
            self.send(net, packet(ServerboundContainerClick { container_id: 0, state_id: state, slot: p.slot, button: p.button, input: p.input, rest: rest.into_bytes() }, State.Play))
        }
    }

    // The step `dig_at` of `dig`, `dig-creative`, `place` or `place-creative`, in a step of its
    // own: each of its packets.
    fn dig(mut self, net: Net, now: u64) {
        let d = steps_of(self.scenario)[self.dig_at].copy()
        // A step whose packets the server's clock times has no name, as each of them marks its own.
        if not d.name.is_empty() {
            self.step(d.name.copy(), now)
        }
        for p in d.packets {
            match p {
                Dug.Action(action, x, y, z, direction, sequence) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPlayerAction { action: action, pos: BlockPos { x: x, y: y, z: z }, direction: u8.wrap(direction), sequence: sequence }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Hold(slot) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundSetCarriedItem { slot: slot }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Use(hand, x, y, z, face, cx, cy, cz, sequence) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundUseItemOn { hand: hand, pos: BlockPos { x: x, y: y, z: z }, direction: face, cursor_x: cx, cursor_y: cy, cursor_z: cz, inside: false, border: false, sequence: sequence }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Turn(y_rot, x_rot) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundMovePlayerRot { y_rot: y_rot, x_rot: x_rot, flags: ON_GROUND }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Give(slot, item) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundSetCreativeModeSlot { slot: slot, stack: untrusted(item, 1, none, []) }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Shift(held) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPlayerInput { flags: if held { 32u8 } else { 0u8 } }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Click(id, c) => {
                    var rest = Writer.new()
                    rest.varint(i32.wrap(c.changed.len()))
                    for (slot, stack) in c.changed {
                        rest.i16(slot)
                        rest.raw(stack)
                    }
                    rest.raw(c.carried)
                    let state = if c.state >= 0 { c.state } else if id == 0 { self.menu_state } else { self.box_state }
                    self.send(net, packet(ServerboundContainerClick { container_id: id, state_id: state, slot: c.slot, button: c.button, input: c.input, rest: rest.into_bytes() }, State.Play))
                },
                Dug.Close(id) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundContainerClose { container_id: id }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Command(text) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundChatCommand { command: String(text) }, State.Play)),
                Dug.Move(x, y, z) => self.moves.push((x, y, z)),
                Dug.Feed(sheep, k, at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.Feed(sheep, k))),
                Dug.Hit(sheep, k, at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.Hit(sheep, k))),
                Dug.HoldAt(slot, at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.Hold(slot))),
                Dug.HitItem(k, at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.HitItem(k))),
                Dug.SprintAt(on, at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.Sprint(on))),
                Dug.MoveAt(x, y, z, ground, at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.Move(x, y, z, ground))),
                Dug.Mark(at, step) => self.timed.push((at, String(step), Timed.Mark)),
                Dug.Leave(at) => self.leave_at = at,
            }
        }
    }

    // What a step the server's clock times sends (D415, D416).
    fn act(mut self, net: Net, act: Timed) {
        match act {
            Timed.Mark => {},
            Timed.Feed(sheep, k) => self.feed(net, sheep, k),
            Timed.Hit(sheep, k) => {
                let ids = if sheep { self.sheep.copy() } else { self.cows.copy() }
                if k < ids.len() {
                    self.send(net, packet(ServerboundAttack { entity_id: ids[k] }, State.Play))
                }
            },
            Timed.Hold(slot) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundSetCarriedItem { slot: slot }, State.Play)),
            Timed.Sprint(on) => self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPlayerCommand { entity_id: 0, action: if on { 1 } else { 2 }, data: 0 }, State.Play)),
            Timed.HitItem(k) => {
                if k < self.items.len() {
                    let id = self.items[k]
                    self.send(net, packet(ServerboundAttack { entity_id: id }, State.Play))
                }
            },
            Timed.Move(x, y, z, ground) => {
                self.x = x
                self.y = y
                self.z = z
                self.send(net, packet(ServerboundMovePlayerPos { x: x, y: y, z: z, flags: if ground { ON_GROUND } else { 0u8 } }, State.Play))
                self.send(net, packet(ServerboundClientTickEnd {}, State.Play))
            },
        }
    }

    // A use of the main hand's stack on the `k`th sheep the server sent, or the `k`th cow
    // (CAL-158).
    fn feed(mut self, net: Net, sheep: bool, k: usize) {
        let ids = if sheep { self.sheep.copy() } else { self.cows.copy() }
        if k < ids.len() {
            var rest = List<u8>()
            // Where on it the bot looks, `LpVec3`'s zero, then no sneaking.
            rest.push(0u8)
            rest.push(0u8)
            self.send(net, packet(ServerboundInteract { entity_id: ids[k], hand: 0, rest: rest }, State.Play))
        }
    }

    // A tick of the client's: the next block of the walk, and the step's end once the server
    // has settled.
    // Whether it only watches, `watch`, or `watch-late` (D431).
    fn watching(self) -> bool {
        return self.scenario == "watch" or self.scenario == "watch-late"
    }

    fn tick(mut self, net: Net, now: u64, view_chunks: u64) {
        if self.done {
            return
        }
        let limit = if self.watching() { STEP_LIMIT + u64.wrap(WATCH) * TICK_NS } else { STEP_LIMIT }
        if now - self.step_at > limit {
            self.mark(String("timeout"))
            self.done = true
            return
        }
        // The next of a step's moves, which keeps the step going until they're made.
        if not self.moves.is_empty() and not self.closed {
            let (x, y, z) = self.moves[0]
            _ = self.moves.remove(0)
            self.x = x
            self.y = y
            self.z = z
            self.send(net, packet(ServerboundMovePlayerPos { x: x, y: y, z: z, flags: ON_GROUND }, State.Play))
            self.heard_at = now
        }
        let settled = now - self.heard_at >= SETTLE and self.timed.is_empty() and self.leave_at < 0
        match self.phase {
            Phase.Before => {
                if self.closed and settled {
                    self.done = true
                }
                return
            },
            Phase.Join => {
                if self.chunks >= view_chunks and not self.loaded {
                    self.loaded = true
                    // `watch-late` never says its client's loaded, so both servers take it as
                    // loaded 60 ticks after it joined, at the same game time (D431).
                    if self.scenario != "watch-late" {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundPlayerLoaded {}, State.Play))
                    }
                }
                if self.loaded and settled and steps_of(self.scenario).len() > 0 {
                    self.phase = Phase.Dig
                    self.dig_at = 0
                    self.dig(net, now)
                } else if self.loaded and settled and self.scenario == "clicks" {
                    self.phase = Phase.Clicks
                    self.click_at = 0
                    self.click(net, now)
                } else if self.loaded and settled and self.scenario == "creative" {
                    self.phase = Phase.Creative
                    self.step(String("creative"), now)
                    for (slot, stack) in creative_slots() {
                        self.send(net, packet(ServerboundSetCreativeModeSlot { slot: slot, stack: stack.copy() }, State.Play))
                    }
                } else if self.loaded and settled and not self.watching() {
                    self.phase = Phase.Walk
                    self.step(String("walk"), now)
                }
            },
            Phase.Walk => {
                if self.walked < WALK {
                    self.walked += 1
                    self.x += 1.0
                    let step = packet(ServerboundMovePlayerPos { x: self.x, y: self.y, z: self.z, flags: ON_GROUND }, State.Play)
                    self.send(net, step)
                } else if settled {
                    self.phase = Phase.Chat
                    self.step(String("chat"), now)
                    let said = ServerboundChat { message: "hello", time_stamp: CHAT_TIME, salt: 0, signature: none, last_seen: LastSeenUpdate.empty() }
                    self.send(net, packet(said, State.Play))
                }
            },
            Phase.Chat => {
                if settled {
                    self.phase = Phase.Command
                    self.step(String("command"), now)
                    self.send(net, packet(ServerboundChatCommand { command: "nonexistent" }, State.Play))
                }
            },
            Phase.Command => {
                if settled {
                    self.phase = Phase.Leave
                    self.step(String("leave"), now)
                    net.close(self.conn)
                    self.closed = true
                    self.done = true
                }
            },
            Phase.Clicks => {
                if settled {
                    self.click_at += 1
                    if self.click_at < clicks().len() {
                        self.click(net, now)
                    } else {
                        self.phase = Phase.Leave
                        self.step(String("leave"), now)
                        net.close(self.conn)
                        self.closed = true
                        self.done = true
                    }
                }
            },
            Phase.Dig => {
                if settled {
                    self.dig_at += 1
                    if self.dig_at < steps_of(self.scenario).len() {
                        self.dig(net, now)
                    } else {
                        self.phase = Phase.Leave
                        self.step(String("leave"), now)
                        net.close(self.conn)
                        self.closed = true
                        self.done = true
                    }
                }
            },
            Phase.Creative => {
                if settled {
                    self.phase = Phase.Leave
                    self.step(String("leave"), now)
                    net.close(self.conn)
                    self.closed = true
                    self.done = true
                }
            },
            Phase.Leave => {},
        }
        if self.placed and not self.closed {
            self.send(net, packet(ServerboundClientTickEnd {}, State.Play))
        }
    }
}

// Whether a packet named `name` is one a step settles past: the time and keep-alives, which come
// on a clock, entities' moves and turns, which vanilla's mobs send as long as they wander (D377),
// and particles, which a jukebox sends every second as long as it plays (CAL-143).
fn quiet(name: String) -> bool {
    let names: List<str> = ["set_time", "keep_alive", "level_particles", "move_entity_pos", "move_entity_pos_rot", "move_entity_rot", "rotate_head", "set_entity_motion", "entity_position_sync", "teleport_entity"]
    for n in names {
        if name == String(n) {
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

// The network ID of `name` in the built-in registry `registry`.
fn builtin_id(registry: String, name: String) -> i32 {
    let names = builtin_names()
    for i in 0..names.len() {
        if names[i] == registry {
            let entries = builtin_entries(i)
            for j in 0..entries.len() {
                if entries[j] == name {
                    return i32.wrap(j)
                }
            }
        }
    }
    panic("session: there's no {registry} {name}")
}

// A stack as `ItemStack.OPTIONAL_UNTRUSTED_STREAM_CODEC` writes it: its count, then, for more
// than none, its item and its patch, each value after its length, here a `damage`'s varint, then
// each type taken away.
fn untrusted(item: str, count: i32, damage: i32?, removed: List<String>) -> List<u8> {
    var w = Writer.new()
    w.varint(count)
    if count <= 0 {
        return w.into_bytes()
    }
    w.varint(builtin_id("item", String(item)))
    w.varint(if damage == none { 0 } else { 1 })
    w.varint(i32.wrap(removed.len()))
    if let d = damage {
        w.varint(builtin_id("data_component_type", "damage"))
        var value = Writer.new()
        value.varint(d)
        let bytes = value.into_bytes()
        w.varint(i32.wrap(bytes.len()))
        w.raw(bytes)
    }
    for t in removed {
        w.varint(builtin_id("data_component_type", t))
    }
    return w.into_bytes()
}

// A click of `clicks`: its step's name and its packets.
struct Click {
    name: String
    packets: List<Pressed>
}

// One packet of a click: a container click on `slot` with `button`, of the kind `input`, with
// the slots a client says it changed and what its cursor then carries, each a `HashedStack`; from
// a stale state where `stale`; or a close where `close`. In a container's menu, from the state
// given, or the one last sent where it's under 0 (CAL-144).
struct Pressed {
    slot: i16 = 0
    button: i8 = 0
    input: i32 = 0
    changed: List<(i16, List<u8>)> = List<(i16, List<u8>)>()
    carried: List<u8> = List<u8>()
    stale: bool = false
    close: bool = false
    state: i32 = -1
}

// `HashedStack.STREAM_CODEC`: nothing, or an item, its count, the components its patch sets, by
// type, without its namespace, with their values' hashes, as `HashOps` hashes them, and those it
// takes away.
fn hashed(item: str, count: i32, set: List<(String, u32)>, removed: List<String>) -> List<u8> {
    var w = Writer.new()
    if count <= 0 {
        w.u8(0)
        return w.into_bytes()
    }
    w.u8(1)
    w.varint(builtin_id(String("item"), String(item)))
    w.varint(count)
    w.varint(i32.wrap(set.len()))
    for (t, h) in set {
        w.varint(builtin_id(String("data_component_type"), t.copy()))
        w.i32(i32.wrap(h))
    }
    w.varint(i32.wrap(removed.len()))
    for t in removed {
        w.varint(builtin_id(String("data_component_type"), t.copy()))
    }
    return w.into_bytes()
}

fn plain(item: str, count: i32) -> List<u8> {
    return hashed(item, count, [], [])
}

fn nothing() -> List<u8> {
    return plain("air", 0)
}

fn press(slot: i16, button: i8, input: i32, changed: own List<(i16, List<u8>)>, carried: own List<u8>) -> Pressed {
    return Pressed { slot: slot, button: button, input: input, changed: changed, carried: carried }
}

// What `clicks` does, click by click, from the `clicks` configuration's inventory: stone in the
// hotbar's first slot, logs named `Logs` in the inventory's first, a potion in the hotbar's third,
// bread without `food` in its last, and a diamond helmet on. Each lists the slots a vanilla client
// would say changed, but `wrong-cursor`, whose cursor is one stone too many, which the server
// corrects; `stale` is from state 0, so the server sends it all again.
fn clicks() -> List<Click> {
    let logs = hashed("oak_log", 10, [(String("custom_name"), hash_string(String("Logs")))], [])
    let potion = hashed("potion", 1, [(String("potion_contents"), hash_map([(hash_string(String("potion")), hash_string(String("minecraft:swiftness")))]))], [])
    let bread = hashed("bread", 7, [], [String("food")])
    return [
        Click { name: "pick-up", packets: [press(36i16, 0i8, 0, [(36i16, nothing())], plain("stone", 64))] },
        Click { name: "put-down", packets: [press(40i16, 0i8, 0, [(40i16, plain("stone", 64))], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "pick-half", packets: [press(40i16, 1i8, 0, [(40i16, plain("stone", 32))], plain("stone", 32))] },
        Click { name: "put-one", packets: [press(41i16, 1i8, 0, [(41i16, plain("stone", 1))], plain("stone", 31))] },
        Click { name: "merge", packets: [press(40i16, 0i8, 0, [(40i16, plain("stone", 63))], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "shift-click", packets: [press(9i16, 0i8, 1, [(9i16, nothing()), (36i16, logs.copy())], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "hotbar-key", packets: [press(20i16, 2i8, 2, [(38i16, nothing()), (20i16, potion.copy())], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "wrong-cursor", packets: [press(41i16, 0i8, 0, [(41i16, nothing())], plain("stone", 2))] },
        Click { name: "put-back", packets: [press(42i16, 0i8, 0, [(42i16, plain("stone", 1))], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "pick-bread", packets: [press(44i16, 0i8, 0, [(44i16, nothing())], bread.copy())] },
        Click { name: "into-grid", packets: [press(1i16, 0i8, 0, [(1i16, bread.copy())], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "helmet-off", packets: [press(5i16, 0i8, 1, [(5i16, nothing()), (9i16, plain("diamond_helmet", 1))], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "helmet-on", packets: [press(9i16, 0i8, 1, [(9i16, nothing()), (5i16, plain("diamond_helmet", 1))], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "stale", packets: [Pressed { slot: 42i16, button: 0i8, input: 0, changed: [(42i16, nothing())], carried: plain("stone", 1), stale: true }] },
        Click { name: "put-back-again", packets: [press(42i16, 0i8, 0, [(42i16, plain("stone", 1))], nothing())] },
        Click { name: "pick-for-drag", packets: [press(40i16, 0i8, 0, [(40i16, nothing())], plain("stone", 63))] },
        Click { name: "drag", packets: [
            press(-999i16, 0i8, 5, [], plain("stone", 63)),
            press(41i16, 1i8, 5, [], plain("stone", 63)),
            press(43i16, 1i8, 5, [], plain("stone", 63)),
            press(39i16, 1i8, 5, [], plain("stone", 63)),
            press(-999i16, 2i8, 5, [(41i16, plain("stone", 21)), (43i16, plain("stone", 21)), (39i16, plain("stone", 21))], nothing()),
        ] },
        Click { name: "close", packets: [Pressed { close: true }] },
    ]
}

// What `crafts` does, step by step, from the `crafts` configuration's inventory: three oak logs
// in the inventory's first slot, four honey bottles in its fourth, paper in its fifth, gunpowder
// in its sixth, iron ingots in its seventh, sticks in its eighth and cobblestone in its ninth,
// crafted with in the inventory menu's grid, then at the crafting fixture's crafting table at 2,
// -60, 0 (CAL-147). Each click lists the slots a vanilla client would say changed: never the
// result, which a client doesn't work out, and on taking it the grid used up as
// `CraftingRecipe.defaultCraftingReminder` leaves it, a honey bottle's glass bottle put back. A
// crafting table's menu has its result, its 3 by 3 grid, then the inventory's 27 and the
// hotbar's 9. A vanilla client sees a shift-click on a result craft once, the server as many
// times as the grid makes it, so the server sends the rest.
fn crafts() -> List<Dig> {
    let bottle = plain("glass_bottle", 1)
    return [
        Dig { name: "pick-logs", packets: [inventory(9i16, 0i8, 0, [(9i16, nothing())], plain("oak_log", 3))] },
        Dig { name: "one-log", packets: [inventory(1i16, 1i8, 0, [(1i16, plain("oak_log", 1))], plain("oak_log", 2))] },
        Dig { name: "not-taken", packets: [inventory(0i16, 0i8, 0, [], plain("oak_log", 2))] },
        Dig { name: "logs-back", packets: [inventory(9i16, 0i8, 0, [(9i16, plain("oak_log", 2))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "take-planks", packets: [inventory(0i16, 0i8, 0, [(0i16, nothing()), (1i16, nothing())], plain("oak_planks", 4))] },
        Dig { name: "one-plank", packets: [inventory(2i16, 1i8, 0, [(2i16, plain("oak_planks", 1))], plain("oak_planks", 3))] },
        Dig { name: "two-planks", packets: [inventory(4i16, 1i8, 0, [(4i16, plain("oak_planks", 1))], plain("oak_planks", 2))] },
        Dig { name: "planks-away", packets: [inventory(10i16, 0i8, 0, [(10i16, plain("oak_planks", 2))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "shift-sticks", packets: [inventory(0i16, 0i8, 1, [(0i16, nothing()), (2i16, nothing()), (4i16, nothing()), (44i16, plain("stick", 4))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "pick-paper", packets: [inventory(13i16, 0i8, 0, [(13i16, nothing())], plain("paper", 1))] },
        Dig { name: "paper-in", packets: [inventory(1i16, 0i8, 0, [(1i16, plain("paper", 1))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "pick-gunpowder", packets: [inventory(14i16, 0i8, 0, [(14i16, nothing())], plain("gunpowder", 1))] },
        Dig { name: "gunpowder-in", packets: [inventory(3i16, 0i8, 0, [(3i16, plain("gunpowder", 1))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "swap-rocket", packets: [inventory(0i16, 2i8, 2, [(0i16, nothing()), (1i16, nothing()), (3i16, nothing()), (38i16, plain("firework_rocket", 3))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "pick-honey", packets: [inventory(12i16, 0i8, 0, [(12i16, nothing())], plain("honey_bottle", 4))] },
        Dig { name: "honey-1", packets: [inventory(1i16, 1i8, 0, [(1i16, plain("honey_bottle", 1))], plain("honey_bottle", 3))] },
        Dig { name: "honey-2", packets: [inventory(2i16, 1i8, 0, [(2i16, plain("honey_bottle", 1))], plain("honey_bottle", 2))] },
        Dig { name: "honey-3", packets: [inventory(3i16, 1i8, 0, [(3i16, plain("honey_bottle", 1))], plain("honey_bottle", 1))] },
        Dig { name: "honey-4", packets: [inventory(4i16, 1i8, 0, [(4i16, plain("honey_bottle", 1))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "take-honey-block", packets: [inventory(0i16, 0i8, 0, [(0i16, nothing()), (1i16, bottle.copy()), (2i16, bottle.copy()), (3i16, bottle.copy()), (4i16, bottle.copy())], plain("honey_block", 1))] },
        Dig { name: "close", packets: [Dug.Close(0)] },
        Dig { name: "open-table", packets: [on_top(2, -60, 0, 1)] },
        Dig { name: "pick-iron", packets: [at_table(16i16, 0i8, 0, [(16i16, nothing())], plain("iron_ingot", 3))] },
        Dig { name: "iron-1", packets: [at_table(1i16, 1i8, 0, [(1i16, plain("iron_ingot", 1))], plain("iron_ingot", 2))] },
        Dig { name: "iron-2", packets: [at_table(2i16, 1i8, 0, [(2i16, plain("iron_ingot", 1))], plain("iron_ingot", 1))] },
        Dig { name: "iron-3", packets: [at_table(3i16, 1i8, 0, [(3i16, plain("iron_ingot", 1))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "pick-sticks", packets: [at_table(17i16, 0i8, 0, [(17i16, nothing())], plain("stick", 2))] },
        Dig { name: "stick-1", packets: [at_table(5i16, 1i8, 0, [(5i16, plain("stick", 1))], plain("stick", 1))] },
        Dig { name: "stick-2", packets: [at_table(8i16, 1i8, 0, [(8i16, plain("stick", 1))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "shift-pickaxe", packets: [at_table(0i16, 0i8, 1, [(0i16, nothing()), (1i16, nothing()), (2i16, nothing()), (3i16, nothing()), (5i16, nothing()), (8i16, nothing()), (44i16, plain("iron_pickaxe", 1))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "pick-cobblestone", packets: [at_table(18i16, 0i8, 0, [(18i16, nothing())], plain("cobblestone", 8))] },
        // Vanilla sets a drag's slots in the order of a `HashSet` of them, by identity, so in
        // another order each run; any one or two of the top row's three make nothing, so the
        // results on the way are the same whatever the order.
        Dig { name: "drag-cobblestone", packets: [
            at_table(-999i16, 0i8, 5, [], plain("cobblestone", 8)),
            at_table(1i16, 1i8, 5, [], plain("cobblestone", 8)),
            at_table(2i16, 1i8, 5, [], plain("cobblestone", 8)),
            at_table(3i16, 1i8, 5, [], plain("cobblestone", 8)),
            at_table(-999i16, 2i8, 5, [(1i16, plain("cobblestone", 2)), (2i16, plain("cobblestone", 2)), (3i16, plain("cobblestone", 2))], plain("cobblestone", 2)),
        ] },
        Dig { name: "cobblestone-back", packets: [at_table(18i16, 0i8, 0, [(18i16, plain("cobblestone", 2))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "shift-slabs", packets: [at_table(0i16, 0i8, 1, [(0i16, nothing()), (1i16, plain("cobblestone", 1)), (2i16, plain("cobblestone", 1)), (3i16, plain("cobblestone", 1)), (43i16, plain("cobblestone_slab", 6))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "shift-logs", packets: [at_table(10i16, 0i8, 1, [(10i16, nothing()), (1i16, plain("oak_log", 2))], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "close-table", packets: [Dug.Close(1)] },
    ]
}

// A click in the crafting table's menu, the first container's the bot opens, from the state it
// was last sent.
fn at_table(slot: i16, button: i8, input: i32, changed: own List<(i16, List<u8>)>, carried: own List<u8>) -> Dug {
    return Dug.Click(1, press(slot, button, input, changed, carried))
}

// A click in the inventory menu, from the state it was last sent.
fn inventory(slot: i16, button: i8, input: i32, changed: own List<(i16, List<u8>)>, carried: own List<u8>) -> Dug {
    return Dug.Click(0, press(slot, button, input, changed, carried))
}

// A packet of a step of `dig`'s or `place`'s: a player action, by its place in `Action`'s order,
// on the block at x, y, z, from the face with the 3D data value given, with its sequence number;
// the hotbar slot to hold; a use of the hand given, 0 the main and 1 the off, on the block at x,
// y, z, hit on the face given where the floats say, from its least corner, with its sequence
// number; a turn to the yaw and pitch given; a stack of one of the item named set in the
// inventory menu's slot given, as the creative menu sets it; shift held or let go, as the
// client's input says; or a click in the container's menu with the ID given, or its close
// (CAL-144), its state the one last sent where it's under 0.
enum Dug {
    Action(i32, i32, i32, i32, i32, i32)
    Hold(i16)
    Use(i32, i32, i32, i32, i32, f32, f32, f32, i32)
    Turn(f32, f32)
    Give(i16, str)
    Shift(bool)
    Click(i32, Pressed)
    Close(i32)
    // A command typed, which a step that waits sends for the server's answer (CAL-148).
    Command(str)
    // A move to x, y, z on the ground, made in a tick of its own.
    Move(f64, f64, f64)
    // A use of the main hand's stack on the `k`th sheep the server sent, or the `k`th cow, at a
    // game time, in a step of the name given (CAL-158); a step of the name given at a game time;
    // and the leave at a game time (D415).
    Feed(bool, usize, i64, str)
    Mark(i64, str)
    Leave(i64)
    // A hit on the `k`th sheep the server sent, or the `k`th cow, a change of the slot held, and a
    // hit on the `k`th item, each at a game time, in a step of the name given, or the last if
    // it's empty (D416).
    Hit(bool, usize, i64, str)
    HoldAt(i16, i64, str)
    HitItem(usize, i64, str)
    // Sprinting started, or stopped, at a game time, in a step of the name given (D417).
    SprintAt(bool, i64, str)
    // A move to x, y, z, on the ground or not, in a client's tick of its own, at a game time, in
    // a step of the name given (D418).
    MoveAt(f64, f64, f64, bool, i64, str)
}

// What a step the server's clock times sends: nothing, a feed, a hit on an animal, a change of the
// slot held, a hit on an item (D415, D416), sprinting started or stopped (D417), or a move, on
// the ground or not, and the client's tick's end (D418).
enum Timed {
    Mark
    Feed(bool, usize)
    Hit(bool, usize)
    Hold(i16)
    HitItem(usize)
    Sprint(bool)
    Move(f64, f64, f64, bool)
}

// A step of `dig`'s: its name and its packets.
struct Dig {
    name: String
    packets: List<Dug>
}

// `START_DESTROY_BLOCK`, `ABORT_DESTROY_BLOCK` and `STOP_DESTROY_BLOCK` on the block at x, y, z,
// from above, with the sequence number `n`.
fn starting(x: i32, y: i32, z: i32, n: i32) -> Dug {
    return Dug.Action(0, x, y, z, 1, n)
}

fn aborting(x: i32, y: i32, z: i32, n: i32) -> Dug {
    return Dug.Action(2, x, y, z, 1, n)
}

fn stopping(x: i32, y: i32, z: i32, n: i32) -> Dug {
    return Dug.Action(3, x, y, z, 1, n)
}

// What `dig` does, step by step, from the `dig` configuration's inventory, with its sequence
// numbers counting up as a client's do, on the dig fixture: its ground is grass at y -61, under
// spawn protection a block around the spawn, with a bed's foot at 3, -60, 1, an oak door at 3, -60,
// 3, tall grass at 3, -60, 5, a command block at 5, -60, 1 and a tripwire at 5, -60, 3. In
// `dig-creative`, what a player who builds instantly breaks.
fn digs(creative: bool) -> List<Dig> {
    if creative {
        return [
            Dig { name: "break-ground", packets: [starting(2, -61, 0, 1)] },
            Dig { name: "break-bed", packets: [starting(3, -60, 1, 2)] },
            Dig { name: "break-door-top", packets: [starting(3, -59, 3, 3)] },
            Dig { name: "break-tall-grass-top", packets: [starting(3, -59, 5, 4)] },
            Dig { name: "command-block", packets: [starting(5, -60, 1, 5)] },
            Dig { name: "sword", packets: [Dug.Hold(3i16), starting(2, -61, 2, 6)] },
        ]
    }
    return [
        Dig { name: "protected", packets: [starting(1, -61, 0, 1)] },
        Dig { name: "dig-through", packets: [starting(2, -61, 0, 2), stopping(2, -61, 0, 3)] },
        Dig { name: "abort", packets: [starting(2, -61, 2, 4), aborting(2, -61, 2, 5)] },
        Dig { name: "switch", packets: [starting(2, -61, 2, 6), starting(3, -61, 2, 7), aborting(3, -61, 2, 8)] },
        Dig { name: "abort-elsewhere", packets: [starting(2, -61, 2, 9), aborting(3, -61, 2, 10)] },
        Dig { name: "stop-elsewhere", packets: [starting(2, -61, 2, 11), stopping(3, -61, 2, 12), aborting(2, -61, 2, 13)] },
        Dig { name: "out-of-reach", packets: [starting(12, -61, 0, 14)] },
        Dig { name: "shears", packets: [Dug.Hold(1i16), starting(5, -60, 3, 15)] },
        Dig { name: "break-tool", packets: [Dug.Hold(2i16), starting(2, -62, 0, 16), stopping(2, -62, 0, 17)] },
        Dig { name: "swap", packets: [Dug.Hold(0i16), Dug.Action(7, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)] },
    ]
}

// A use of the main hand on the top of the block at x, y, z, hit in its middle, with the sequence
// number `n`.
fn on_top(x: i32, y: i32, z: i32, n: i32) -> Dug {
    return Dug.Use(0, x, y, z, 1, 0.5f32, 1.0f32, 0.5f32, n)
}

// A use of the main hand on the side `face` of the block at x, y, z, hit `up` from its bottom, in
// the middle across.
fn on_side(x: i32, y: i32, z: i32, face: i32, up: f32, n: i32) -> Dug {
    let cx = if face == 4 { 0.0f32 } else if face == 5 { 1.0f32 } else { 0.5f32 }
    let cz = if face == 2 { 0.0f32 } else if face == 3 { 1.0f32 } else { 0.5f32 }
    return Dug.Use(0, x, y, z, face, cx, up, cz, n)
}

// The steps of the scenario, if it's `dig`, `dig-creative`, `place`, `place-creative`, `use`,
// `use-items`, `use-books`, `use-containers` or `crafts`, or none.
fn steps_of(scenario: String) -> List<Dig> {
    if scenario == "dig" or scenario == "dig-creative" {
        return digs(scenario == "dig-creative")
    }
    if scenario == "place" {
        return places()
    }
    if scenario == "place-creative" {
        return creative_places()
    }
    if scenario == "use" {
        return uses()
    }
    if scenario == "use-items" {
        return item_uses()
    }
    if scenario == "use-books" {
        return book_uses()
    }
    if scenario == "use-containers" {
        return container_uses()
    }
    if scenario == "crafts" {
        return crafts()
    }
    if scenario == "items" {
        return item_drops()
    }
    if scenario == "items-saved" {
        return saved_items()
    }
    if scenario == "orbs" {
        return orb_breaks()
    }
    if scenario == "feed" {
        return feeds()
    }
    if scenario == "attack" {
        return attacks()
    }
    if scenario == "sweep" {
        return sweeps()
    }
    if scenario == "fall" {
        return falls()
    }
    if scenario == "checks" {
        return checks()
    }
    return []
}

// What `checks` does on the `checks` fixture's world (D420), at the spawn, by the server's clock:
// at game time 200 a move 12 blocks south in one tick, too quick, which the server sends it back
// from; at 240 one through the wall, which stops it more than a quarter of a block short, wrong;
// at 280 two steps toward the wall and one a little into it, which its box didn't meet before;
// at 320 nine blocks up, by the ladder at the wall's north end, and two north; at 360 down past
// it in moves of a block and a half, a clip of what resets a fall, which forgets the fall
// before it, so the landing doesn't hurt (D422); at 400 five blocks up in half blocks, off the
// ground, where it floats, sending nothing more, till the server kicks it for floating; it'd
// leave at 600.
fn checks() -> List<Dig> {
    let quick: List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)> = [(0.5, -60.0, 12.5, true)]
    let through: List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)> = [(2.8, -60.0, 0.5, true)]
    let into: List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)> = [(1.0, -60.0, 0.5, true), (1.5, -60.0, 0.5, true), (1.9, -60.0, 0.5, true)]
    var climb: List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)> = [(1.5, -59.0, -0.5, false), (1.5, -58.0, -1.5, false)]
    for i in 1..8 {
        climb.push((1.5, -58.0 + f64(i), -1.5, false))
    }
    var fast = List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>()
    for i in 1..7 {
        fast.push((1.5, -51.0 - f64(i) * 1.5, -1.5, i == 6))
    }
    var up = List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>()
    for i in 1..11 {
        up.push((1.5, -60.0 + f64(i) * 0.5, 0.5, false))
    }
    var packets = List<Dug>()
    moves_at(quick, 200, "too-quick", mut packets)
    moves_at(through, 240, "through", mut packets)
    moves_at(into, 280, "into", mut packets)
    moves_at(climb, 320, "climb", mut packets)
    moves_at(fast, 360, "past-ladder", mut packets)
    moves_at(up, 400, "float", mut packets)
    packets.push(Dug.Leave(600))
    return [Dig { name: String(), packets: packets }]
}

// The moves of `path` onto `out`, each in a client's tick of its own, at the game time `at`, the
// first in a step named `step` (D418).
fn moves_at(path: List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>, at: i64, step: str, out: mut List<Dug>) {
    var first = true
    for (x, y, z, ground) in path {
        out.push(Dug.MoveAt(x, y, z, ground, at, if first { step } else { "" }))
        first = false
    }
}

// The ways down of a fall from `y` at x, z, each a move as a client's tick makes it, faster
// each tick to 0.875, the last to `to`, onto the ground where it `lands` (D418). Each is a
// float's eighths, so the fall adds up exactly.
fn falling(x: f64, z: f64, y: f64, to: f64, lands: bool, path: mut List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>) {
    let steps: List<f64> = [0.125, 0.25, 0.375, 0.5, 0.625, 0.75]
    var at = y
    for s in steps {
        if at - s <= to {
            break
        }
        at = at - s
        path.push((x, at, z, false))
    }
    while at - 0.875 > to {
        at = at - 0.875
        path.push((x, at, z, false))
    }
    path.push((x, to, z, lands))
}

// What `fall` does on the `fall` fixture's world (D418), on its pillar 30 up, facing east with an
// iron sword, by the server's clock, each fall under 10 blocks, as vanilla lets a tick's moves
// go: from game time 200 it walks off east and falls nine onto the honey, which takes four
// fifths of the hurt; at 240 off the honey into the basin's water, which forgets the fall; at 280
// it climbs out onto the basin's wall, jumping as it leaves the ground; at 320 it walks off the
// wall and falls nine to the platform, hitting the cow halfway down, a critical hit; then a step
// from 360 as its health comes back, and it leaves at 480.
fn falls() -> List<Dig> {
    var honey = List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>()
    honey.push((0.9, -30.0, 0.5, true))
    honey.push((1.4, -30.0, 0.5, false))
    honey.push((1.8, -30.125, 0.5, false))
    honey.push((2.2, -30.375, 0.5, false))
    honey.push((2.5, -30.75, 0.5, false))
    falling(2.5, 0.5, -30.75, -39.0625, true, mut honey)
    var water = List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>()
    water.push((2.9, -39.0625, 0.5, true))
    water.push((3.4, -39.0625, 0.5, false))
    water.push((3.8, -39.1875, 0.5, false))
    water.push((4.2, -39.4375, 0.5, false))
    water.push((4.6, -39.8125, 0.5, false))
    water.push((5.0, -40.3125, 0.5, false))
    water.push((5.5, -40.9375, 0.5, false))
    falling(5.5, 0.5, -40.9375, -48.0, true, mut water)
    let climb: List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)> = [(6.2, -48.0, 0.5, true), (6.2, -47.5, 0.5, false), (6.6, -47.0, 0.5, false), (7.3, -47.0, 0.5, true)]
    var down = List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>()
    down.push((7.7, -47.0, 0.5, true))
    down.push((8.4, -47.0, 0.5, false))
    falling(8.4, 0.5, -47.0, -51.5, false, mut down)
    var rest = List<(f64, f64, f64, bool)>()
    falling(8.4, 0.5, -51.5, -56.0, true, mut rest)
    var packets = List<Dug>()
    moves_at(honey, 200, "honey", mut packets)
    moves_at(water, 240, "water", mut packets)
    moves_at(climb, 280, "climb", mut packets)
    moves_at(down, 320, "crit-fall", mut packets)
    packets.push(Dug.Hit(false, 0, 320, ""))
    moves_at(rest, 320, "", mut packets)
    packets.push(Dug.Mark(360, "after"))
    packets.push(Dug.Leave(480))
    return [Dig { name: String(), packets: packets }]
}

// What `sweep` does on the `sweep` fixture's world (D417), at the spawn facing east with an iron
// sword, by the server's clock from game time 200: the sheep hit whole, which sweeps the cows by
// it, and again in the same tick, too weak to do anything or sweep; sprinting started; the first
// cow hit as it sprints, a knockback attack, which doesn't sweep, and stops its sprint; then the
// second cow, the sheep and the cows hit in turn, each sweeping the rest, till all are dead; then,
// from game time 380, a step as their loot lies and their orbs come to it, till it leaves at 520.
fn sweeps() -> List<Dig> {
    return [
        Dig { name: String(), packets: [
            Dug.Hit(true, 0, 200, "sweep-sheep"),
            Dug.Hit(true, 0, 200, ""),
            Dug.SprintAt(true, 220, "sprint"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 0, 240, "knock-first-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 1, 260, "sweep-second-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(true, 0, 280, "sweep-sheep-again"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 0, 300, "sweep-first-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 1, 320, "sweep-second-cow-again"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 0, 340, "hit-first-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 1, 360, "hit-second-cow"),
            Dug.Mark(380, "after"),
            Dug.Leave(520),
        ] },
    ]
}

// What `attack` does on the `attack` fixture's world (D416), at the spawn facing east, its hand
// empty and a stone axe in the second slot, by the server's clock, which it hears every 20 ticks,
// from game time 200, well after the join: the first cow the server sent punched for 1, and again
// in the same tick, too weak to beat what its cooldown holds; the axe taken; the sheep chopped as
// the axe has charged most of the way, and again in the same tick; the first cow killed, its beef,
// leather and orbs dropped; the sheep killed; the second cow chopped, then killed; then, from game
// time 420, a step as the dead are taken away and their orbs come to the bot, which then hits the
// first item the server sent at game time 540, so it's disconnected, each step within the limit.
fn attacks() -> List<Dig> {
    return [
        Dig { name: String(), packets: [
            Dug.Hit(false, 0, 200, "punch-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 0, 200, ""),
            Dug.HoldAt(1, 220, "hold-axe"),
            Dug.Hit(true, 0, 240, "chop-sheep"),
            Dug.Hit(true, 0, 240, ""),
            Dug.Hit(false, 0, 280, "kill-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(true, 0, 320, "kill-sheep"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 1, 360, "chop-second-cow"),
            Dug.Hit(false, 1, 400, "kill-second-cow"),
            Dug.Mark(420, "after"),
            Dug.HitItem(0, 540, "hit-item"),
        ] },
    ]
}

// What `feed` does on the `feed` fixture's world (CAL-158), at the spawn facing east with wheat,
// by the server's clock, 40 ticks apart from game time 200, well after the join (D415): the cows
// fed in the order the server sent them, a calf that grows older and two grown that fall in love,
// whichever comes where; the sheep, which fall in love; the first cow again; then, from game time
// 440, a step as each pair breeds, its orb comes to the bot and the babies follow their parents,
// till the bot leaves at game time 720, each step within the step limit.
fn feeds() -> List<Dig> {
    return [
        Dig { name: String(), packets: [
            Dug.Feed(false, 0, 200, "feed-cow"),
            Dug.Feed(false, 1, 240, "feed-cow-again"),
            Dug.Feed(false, 2, 280, "feed-third-cow"),
            Dug.Feed(true, 0, 320, "feed-sheep"),
            Dug.Feed(true, 1, 360, "feed-sheep-again"),
            Dug.Feed(false, 0, 400, "feed-cow-last"),
            Dug.Mark(440, "breed"),
            Dug.Leave(720),
        ] },
    ]
}

// What `orbs` does, step by step, on the `orbs` fixture's world (CAL-154), at the spawn facing east
// with a diamond hoe with mending, one use off whole: the sculk at 2, -60, 0, which it breaks at
// once, then that north and south of it, each worth an orb of 1, which follow it and are picked
// up, mending the hoe first; then the sculk catalyst at 3, -60, 0, let go too soon so it's dug
// the rest of the way, worth 5, split into orbs of 3, 1 and 1.
fn orb_breaks() -> List<Dig> {
    return [
        Dig { name: "sculk", packets: [starting(2, -60, 0, 1)] },
        Dig { name: "wait", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "sculk-north", packets: [starting(2, -60, -1, 2)] },
        Dig { name: "sculk-south", packets: [starting(2, -60, 1, 3)] },
        Dig { name: "wait-more", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "catalyst", packets: [starting(3, -60, 0, 4), stopping(3, -60, 0, 5)] },
        Dig { name: "wait-after", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "wait-last", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
    ]
}

// What `items-saved` does, step by step, on the `items_saved` fixture's world (CAL-148): diamonds
// at 0.5, -60, 3.5, oak logs that can't be picked up at 5.5, stone that's another's at 7.5, and a
// sword out of the way. It waits, then walks south over them from the spawn, a block a tick.
fn saved_items() -> List<Dig> {
    var walk = List<Dug>()
    for i in 1..17 {
        walk.push(Dug.Move(0.5, -60.0, 0.5 + f64(i) * 0.5))
    }
    return [
        Dig { name: "wait", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "wait-more", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "walk", packets: walk },
        Dig { name: "wait-after", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
    ]
}

// What `items` does, step by step, from the `items` configuration's inventory (CAL-148): stone in
// the hotbar's first slot, which the bot holds, dirt in its second, an iron sword in its third and
// oak logs in the inventory's first. The bot stands on the flat world's ground at 0.5, -60, 0.5,
// facing south, which most of its drops go, the stone it throws east, and walks south over them
// once they can be picked up.
fn item_drops() -> List<Dig> {
    var walk = List<Dug>()
    for i in 1..9 {
        walk.push(Dug.Move(0.5, -60.0, 0.5 + f64(i) * 0.5))
    }
    return [
        Dig { name: "drop-one", packets: [Dug.Action(5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)] },
        Dig { name: "drop-all", packets: [Dug.Hold(1i16), Dug.Action(4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)] },
        Dig { name: "pick-logs", packets: [inventory(9i16, 0i8, 0, [(9i16, nothing())], plain("oak_log", 5))] },
        Dig { name: "throw-logs", packets: [inventory(-999i16, 1i8, 0, [], plain("oak_log", 4)), inventory(-999i16, 0i8, 0, [], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "throw-key", packets: [Dug.Turn(-90.0f32, 0.0f32), inventory(36i16, 0i8, 4, [(36i16, plain("stone", 62))], nothing()), inventory(36i16, 1i8, 4, [(36i16, nothing())], nothing())] },
        Dig { name: "drop-sword", packets: [Dug.Turn(90.0f32, 30.0f32), Dug.Hold(2i16), Dug.Action(5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)] },
        Dig { name: "turn-back", packets: [Dug.Turn(0.0f32, 0.0f32), Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "wait", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "wait-more", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
        Dig { name: "walk", packets: walk },
        Dig { name: "wait-after", packets: [Dug.Command("nonexistent")] },
    ]
}

// A click in a container's menu just opened, from its first state, 1.
fn fresh(slot: i16, button: i8, input: i32, changed: own List<(i16, List<u8>)>, carried: own List<u8>) -> Pressed {
    return Pressed { slot: slot, button: button, input: input, changed: changed, carried: carried, state: 1 }
}

// What `use-containers` does, step by step, from the `use_containers` configuration's inventory:
// stone in the hotbar's first slot, which the bot holds, and dirt in its second. The containers
// fixture has a chest facing west at 2, -60, 0 with diamonds in its first slot; a large chest
// facing east, its right half at -2, -60, 1 with gold and its left at -2, -60, 0 with iron in its
// sixth slot; a trapped chest facing north at 0, -60, 2 with a lamp east of it; a barrel facing up
// at 0, -60, -2 with cobblestone; an ender chest at -2, -60, -2; a shulker box facing up at 2,
// -60, -2; a dispenser facing up at -2, -60, 2 with arrows in its middle slot; a hopper at 2, -60,
// 2; and a chest at 1, -60, -3 under stone. A chest's menu has its 27 slots, then the
// inventory's 27, then the hotbar's 9; a large chest's 54, a dispenser's 9.
fn container_uses() -> List<Dig> {
    return [
        Dig { name: "chest", packets: [
            on_side(2, -60, 0, 4, 0.5f32, 1),
            Dug.Click(1, fresh(0i16, 0i8, 0, [(0i16, nothing())], plain("diamond", 3))),
            Dug.Click(1, fresh(27i16, 0i8, 0, [(27i16, plain("diamond", 3))], nothing())),
            Dug.Click(1, fresh(54i16, 0i8, 1, [(54i16, nothing()), (0i16, plain("stone", 10))], nothing())),
            Dug.Close(1),
        ] },
        Dig { name: "large-chest", packets: [
            on_side(-2, -60, 0, 5, 0.5f32, 2),
